-- Three packages, one project (ADR-0005). The Producer and the Verifier share
-- no format logic: `eventchain-verify` must never build-depend on
-- `eventchain`, because a Verifier that imports the Producer's canonicalizer
-- attests self-consistency rather than conformance. That edge's absence is
-- what makes the golden vectors evidence, so `cabal test all` asserts it
-- (gates:verifier-independence) rather than trusting this comment.
--
-- Crypto goes the other way: `eventchain-crypto` is shared by both, because
-- there agreement is the requirement rather than the question, and a
-- known-answer test against OpenSSL gates it without needing a dissenter.
--
-- `gates` is not a fourth part of the system; it is the part that grades the
-- other three. It ships nothing and nothing depends on it. Its test suites are
-- what make the paragraph above true rather than aspirational, so they run
-- whenever the tests do.
packages:
    eventchain-crypto
    eventchain
    eventchain-verify
    gates
